Free Aitong Medical Camp

Healing in the Heart of Mara

Kicheche Community Trust in partnership with Saruni Basecamp and Safarilin=
k=2C organised a free medical camp at CHP Aitong Clinic. It was a beacon o=
f hope and care for the Aitong community providing vital healthcare servic=
es to 886 patients over three impactful days.

This life-changing initiative=2C made possible by the incredible dedicatio=
n of volunteer doctors and conservation partners=2C addressed various medi=
cal needs=2C from general consultations=2C and pediatric care to dental ch=
eck-ups=2C nutrition=2C gynecology services=2C and HPV testing.

Nanny=2C Dr. Geert=2C Ledama & Dr. Pol - Dental Team

Dr. Luis & Joshua - HPV Testing & Gynaecology

Inge - Registration & Triage

Among the standout contributors was 14 year old Leshan=2C son of Kicheche=
 Mara=E2=80=99s guide Jimmy Tinka. Leshan=E2=80=99s enthusiasm and commitm=
ent at the triage section was inspiring=2C showcasing the power of communi=
ty spirit across all ages.

Leshan taking patients=E2=80=99 temperature.

Leshan with the father=2C Jimmy Tinka.

We extend our heartfelt gratitude to every individual who supported this c=
amp. Your efforts are healing today=E2=80=99s patients and building health=
ier=2C brighter futures for the Aitong community.

Women Empowerment Program

Empowering Women=2C Enriching Communities

Kicheche Community Trust proudly concluded the annual transformative Women=
 Empowerment Training Program at the Maasai Mara Wildlife Conservancies As=
sociation (MMWCA)=2C near Mara North Conservancy. The two-week initiative=
 brought together 21 determined women eager to acquire life-changing skill=
s and build brighter futures for themselves and their communities.

The training covered a diverse range of topics=2C including:
* Family Planning & Female genital mutilation (FGM) Awareness
* Storekeeping & Clerical Skills
* Mental Health & Personal Branding
* Business & Budgeting
* Computer Skills & Sewing
* Kitchen Gardening

Elisa=2C Inge & Nanny - Volunteer Trainers

Participants engaging in a group activity.

We owe immense gratitude to our incredible volunteer trainers =E2=80=93 El=
isa=2C Inge=2C Nanny=2C and Julius =E2=80=93 for their unwavering dedicati=
on and passion. Their expertise and encouragement inspired the participant=
s to unlock their potential and embrace opportunities with confidence.

A heartfelt thank you also goes to MMWCA=2C our hosting partner=2C for pro=
viding the space and support that made this program possible.

